{"name":"Dirty Leather","hex":"#430005","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dirty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Unclean; covered with or containing unpleasant substances such as dirt or grime.","That makes one unclean; corrupting, infecting."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In a dirty manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dirty"},{"term":"leather","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tough material produced from the skin of animals, by tanning or similar process, used e.g. for clothing; often denotes leather from cattle when no qualifier specifies otherwise.","A piece of the above used for polishing."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of leather.","Referring to one who wears leather clothing (motorcycle jacket, chaps over 501 jeans, boots), especially as a sign of sadomasochistic homosexuality."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leather"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dirt","blocks":[{"text":"Dirt  is any matter considered unclean, especially when in contact with a person's clothes, skin, or possessions. In such cases, they are said to become dirty.\nCommon types of dirt include:"},{"items":["Debris: scattered pieces of waste or remains","Dust: a general powder of organic or mineral matter","Filth: foul matter such as excrement","Grime: a black, ingrained dust such as soot","Soil: the mix of clay, sand, and humus which lies on top of bedrock. The term 'soil' may be used to refer to unwanted substances or dirt that are deposited onto surfaces such as clothing."]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/King%27s_Cross%2C_London%3B_the_Great_Dust-Heap%2C_next_to_Battle_Br_Wellcome_V0013642.jpg/330px-King%27s_Cross%2C_London%3B_the_Great_Dust-Heap%2C_next_to_Battle_Br_Wellcome_V0013642.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dirt"},{"title":"Leather","blocks":[{"text":"Leather is a strong, flexible and durable material obtained from the tanning, or chemical treatment, of animal skins and hides to prevent decay. The most common leathers come from cattle, sheep, goats, equine animals, buffalo, pigs and hogs, ostriches, and aquatic animals such as seals and alligators."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Leathertools.jpg/330px-Leathertools.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leather"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Dirty_Dick%27s_-_geograph.org.uk_-_821364.jpg/330px-Dirty_Dick%27s_-_geograph.org.uk_-_821364.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Dirty_Dick%27s_-_geograph.org.uk_-_821364.jpg/330px-Dirty_Dick%27s_-_geograph.org.uk_-_821364.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dirty Dicks is a Bishopsgate pub named after Dirty Dick, who once owned it and was notoriously filthy.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADirty_Dick's_-_geograph.org.uk_-_821364.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Sure_We_Can_Earthday_clean_2021_1.jpg/500px-Sure_We_Can_Earthday_clean_2021_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Sure_We_Can_Earthday_clean_2021_1.jpg/1280px-Sure_We_Can_Earthday_clean_2021_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Sure_We_Can_Earthday_clean_2021_1.jpg/500px-Sure_We_Can_Earthday_clean_2021_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dirt-covered sidewalk in Brooklyn, NYC being swept during a community clean-up","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASure_We_Can